Article 96-2 (Informatization of local government finance) (1) Unless grounds prescribed by Presidential Decree exist, the head of a local government shall conduct all the affairs concerning local government finance through an information system prescribed by the Minister of the Interior and Safety. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017>
  (2) The Minister of the Interior and Safety shall develop and operate an information system necessary for the disclosure of the management conditions of local government finance and consolidated publication under Article 60-2. In such cases, he or she may include the conditions of business management of local public enterprises and local government-invested or -funded institutions. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017>
  (3) The Minister of the Interior and Safety may request related institutions to provide information necessary to conduct affairs under paragraph (2). In such cases, any institution, in receipt of a request, shall comply with such request. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; Jul. 26, 2017>
  [This Article Added on May 28, 2014]

Article 96-3 (Education for public officials related to local government finance) The Minister of the Interior and Safety and the head of a local government may conduct education for public officials related to local government finance, as prescribed by Presidential Decree, for the sound and efficient management of local government finance. <Amended on Nov. 19, 2014; May 29, 2016; Jul. 26, 2017>
